{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":139541,"duration_api_ms":308719,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6c2a7ac1-34ec-4ced-a806-9aa527862508","total_cost_usd":0.95152115,"usage":{"input_tokens":6166,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34099,"cache_read_input_tokens":80647,"output_tokens":3958,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34099,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2852,"outputTokens":21232,"cacheReadInputTokens":2217569,"cacheCreationInputTokens":190024,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5682989,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6166,"outputTokens":3958,"cacheReadInputTokens":80647,"cacheCreationInputTokens":34099,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.38322225,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accepted three amendments addressing real correctness and maintainability issues: the NH3 label inconsistency against the canonical UNITS.md spec, the deserialization compatibility gap where legacy alias logic lives only in the TUI client rather than tank_core, and the TDS/conductivity divergence between cached state accessors and fresh-solve snapshot values. Rejected the unused conversions module and GH precision change amendments as they do not identify concrete correctness or safety defects.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-c9fd9fff","decision":"reject","rationale":"The module is declared `pub mod conversions` and is therefore part of the public library API surface — the absence of in-repo callers does not make it dead code in the usual sense. It is thoroughly documented in UNITS.md as the canonical conversion API for display-layer consumers. The module is correctly implemented and comprehensively tested internally. This is a 'feature not yet integrated into the TUI/API' situation, not a correctness or safety defect. The amendment's recommendation to add `pub use conversions::*` would be a nice ergonomic improvement but does not fix a bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-b753cd38","decision":"reject","rationale":"GH is never directly persisted — saves store the underlying calcium_mg_total and magnesium_mg_total, and GH is always recomputed on demand via gh_d(). Since the same formula is applied consistently within any single codebase version, save/load roundtrip produces identical GH values. The ~0.05% drift only manifests when comparing values computed by different versions of the code, which is expected behavior for a precision refinement. The StabilityTracker does persist prev_gh_d, but a 0.0005 dGH ghost delta on first tick after a version upgrade is negligible relative to the stress thresholds. A tolerance test would be nice hardening but the amendment does not identify a substantive correctness bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-2b018d6f","decision":"accept","rationale":"The inconsistency is clear and verifiable: overview.rs labels the quantity as 'mg N/L' while chemistry.rs labels the same field as 'mg NH3-N/L'. docs/UNITS.md defines the canonical public label as 'Free NH3-N (mg NH3-N/L)'. Users comparing the overview and chemistry screens will see different unit notation for the identical value (nh3_mg_n_per_l), which is confusing. The fix is straightforward: standardize overview.rs to use 'mg NH3-N/L' to match the canonical spec and the chemistry screen."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-84ddc83e","decision":"accept","rationale":"The LEGACY_SNAPSHOT_CHEMISTRY_FIELD_ALIASES constant is defined in tank_core, yet the actual compatibility normalization is implemented only in the TUI client's api_client.rs. Any other Rust consumer deserializing a legacy-only JSON payload directly into TankSnapshot will fail because the struct has no serde(alias) attributes. While today there is only one consumer (TUI), the architectural layering is wrong: the alias table and the compatibility logic that uses it should live in the same crate. Adding #[serde(alias = \"tan_mg_l\")] etc. to TankSnapshot fields would be a clean, zero-overhead fix that prevents every future consumer from having to reimplement the normalization shim."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-83b30b59","decision":"accept","rationale":"Two public API paths for TDS/conductivity can return different values for the same TankState: TankState::tds_mg_per_l() uses cached bicarbonate_mg_total while TankSnapshot::estimated_tds_7_ion_mg_per_l uses a fresh carbonate equilibrium solve. The test at snapshot.rs:256-289 explicitly asserts this divergence (snapshot > cached), which locks it in as intended behavior rather than treating it as a bug to be fixed. This is a maintenance trap — any internal caller using the state accessor instead of going through TankSnapshot will silently get stale TDS/conductivity values. The fix should either refresh the cache before the public accessor or factor the fresh carbonate projection into a shared helper so both paths converge."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"91db7754-a7ba-420f-baba-78db4d04d7a3"}
